WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:09.630
With SuiFleet, managing your devices is simple. Bring your
devices together, organize them into groups, and keep their
software up to date from one console.

2
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:21.758
You choose what changes, and which devices receive it. Your
wallet acts as a secure approval app. It confirms your
permission, without sharing your private key.

3
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:35.465
Sui saves your approval on a shared network. Walrus stores your
software files for the period you choose. Private releases are
encrypted, with access limited to authorized devices.

4
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:46.974
The SuiFleet client on each device checks for approved updates
on its configured schedule. Connections start from the device,
so you do not need to open an incoming connection.

5
00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:59.358
When an update is available, the device downloads it from Walrus
and verifies that it matches the approved release. A device that
reconnects can catch up while the update remains available.

6
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:10.995
SuiFleet then runs your configured installer. Your platform
handles installation, any reboot, and recovery. This lets you
use the update process that suits your devices.

7
00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:22.313
See which installations succeeded and which failed. Device
health is reported separately. If an update fails, review the
available diagnostics before trying again.

8
00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:34.014
Start with a small group, check the results, and expand your
rollout in stages. You stay in control of the release, while
SuiFleet coordinates delivery across your fleet.

9
00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:38.121
Start your SuiFleet journey today.
